WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:02.520
Hello everyone!

2
00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.370
How are you today?

3
00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.541
I'm very happy to see you.

4
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:16.590
Look what I have. It's a rainbow. But wait, there are no colors.

5
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.140
Can you help me put the colors back?

6
00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.640
Yes! Let's make a beautiful rainbow together.

7
00:00:25.651 --> 00:00:27.661
First, let's look at what we need.

8
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:34.981
We need our rainbow worksheet. Can you say, "rainbow worksheet?"

9
00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.490
Brilliant! We need some little pieces of colored paper.

10
00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.610
Can you say, "colored paper?"

11
00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.880
Nice! Wow! Look at all these colors.

12
00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:08.640
We have red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and pink.

13
00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:13.980
And we need some glue. Can you say, "glue?"

14
00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:27.750
Well done! Teacher, may we have the materials, please?

15
00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:30.780
Do you have everything?

16
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.770
Great. Let's get ready.

17
00:01:36.391 --> 00:01:38.370
Before we begin, watch here.

18
00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:42.180
First, put some glue on the rainbow.

19
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:44.490
Just a little.

20
00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:54.360
Next, pick up one piece of colored paper, put it on the rainbow, and

21
00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:55.051
press.

22
00:01:57.301 --> 00:02:01.290
Glue, put, and press. Now you know what to do.

23
00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:04.980
Let's begin with the first color.

24
00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.410
What color is this?

25
00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.300
It's red.

26
00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:14.550
Let's say it together.

27
00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:16.380
Red.

28
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:26.460
Great speaking.

29
00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.050
Put some glue on the red part of your rainbow.

30
00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.900
Now add your red paper pieces.

31
00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.921
Glue, put, and press.

32
00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:45.150
Keep going.

33
00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.880
Fantastic! Your red rainbow stripe looks great.

34
00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.050
Now we need our next color.

35
00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.880
It's orange. Let's say it together.

36
00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:01.921
Orange.

37
00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:11.580
Well done.

38
00:03:13.139 --> 00:03:15.150
Add a little glue to the orange stripe.

39
00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.180
Now add your orange paper pieces.

40
00:03:23.101 --> 00:03:24.360
Press them down gently.

41
00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:34.800
Lovely orange.

42
00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.510
Look at this bright color.

43
00:03:41.791 --> 00:03:44.520
It looks like the sun. What color is it?

44
00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:52.380
It's yellow. Let's say it together. Yellow.

45
00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:01.980
Excellent.

46
00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.090
Put some glue on the yellow stripe.

47
00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:17.760
Now add your yellow paper pieces. Glue, put, and press.

48
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.820
Great job. Your rainbow is getting brighter.

49
00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.290
Here comes our next color.

50
00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:37.201
What color is it?

51
00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:45.360
It's green. Let's say it together. Green.

52
00:04:54.091 --> 00:04:55.020
Nice speaking.

53
00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.770
Add a little glue to the green stripe.

54
00:05:05.281 --> 00:05:09.000
Now add your green paper pieces. Keep going.

55
00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.091
Wow, that green looks wonderful.

56
00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:32.580
Oh, a little raindrop. What color is it?

57
00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:38.040
It's blue.

58
00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.350
Let's say it together.

59
00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:42.240
Blue.

60
00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:51.480
Great job.

61
00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.050
Put some glue on the blue stripe.

62
00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:04.201
Now add your blue paper pieces.

63
00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.920
Press, press, press.

64
00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.281
Beautiful blue.

65
00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:21.810
We have one more color.

66
00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.331
Can you guess what it is?

67
00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:32.490
It's pink. Let's say it together. Pink.

68
00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:41.610
Perfect.

69
00:06:43.561 --> 00:06:45.480
Add a little glue to the pink stripe.

70
00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:53.730
This is our last color. Keep going. You're almost finished.

71
00:07:06.331 --> 00:07:07.440
Wonderful work.

72
00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:16.530
We did it! Look at our beautiful rainbows.

73
00:07:18.151 --> 00:07:22.980
Our rainbows have all their colors again. Hold up your rainbow and show me.

74
00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:29.401
Wow! They look fantastic.

75
00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:36.841
You did a wonderful job today. You listened carefully, practiced your colors,

76
00:07:37.081 --> 00:07:41.520
and made a beautiful rainbow. Give yourself a big clap.

77
00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:50.040
Thank you for making a rainbow with me. See you next time. Bye-bye!
